# .licensing-tiers — path -> licensing tier map for GSys LibreCore.
#
# Format:  <TIER> <whitespace> <glob>          (one glob per line; '#' comments)
# Tiers:   R  LibreCore-original  -> CERN-OHL-S-2.0 OR LicenseRef-GSys-Commercial
#          T  tooling/docs        -> MIT
#          U  upstream/third-party-> unchanged, preserve verbatim
#          F  GPL firmware        -> GPL-2.0-or-later, separate work
#          P  withheld, two cases:
#             case 1 NDA / foundry PDK      -> LicenseRef-Proprietary
#             case 2 commercial-only G6LC   -> LicenseRef-GSys-Commercial
#
# Resolution: LAST matching rule wins, so specific rules follow general ones.
# U is asserted explicitly for whole subtrees to make E-UPSTREAMWRITE enforceable.
# Governed by AGENTS-licensing.md. Consumed by `build.sh diag run licensing`.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ default ---
# Anything not otherwise classified is treated as upstream and left alone.
U   **

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- tier U ---
# Vendored / submodule / third-party subtrees. Never relicense, never rename,
# never alter a copyright, SPDX or attribution line inside these.
U   vendor/**
U   core/cvfpu/**
U   core/cache_subsystem/hpdcache/**
U   corev_apu/riscv-dbg/**
U   corev_apu/axi_mem_if/**
U   corev_apu/fpga/src/ariane-ethernet/**
U   verif/core-v-verif/**
U   common/**
U   config/**
U   util/**

