P   pdk/**

# ------------------------------------------------------------- tier P case 2 ---
# LibreCore-original material deliberately WITHHELD from the open path ->
# LicenseRef-GSys-Commercial alone, no "OR CERN-OHL-S-2.0".
#
# This tier is a MECHANISM that remains available; it currently classifies NO
# path. It is kept defined so that a future subsystem can be withheld without
# re-deriving the policy, and so LICENSE.GSys-Commercial 4.5 has a referent.
#
# IRREVERSIBLE, if ever used: publishing a path under CERN-OHL-S-2.0 even once
# grants rights in that version permanently. Classify BEFORE the first commit
# of the file, never after.
#
# (no tier P case 2 globs are active)

# ------------------------------------------------- AI matrix plane (Xg6lcai) ---
# DELIBERATELY ON THE NORMAL OPEN PATH. The AI implementation is tier R, i.e.
# "CERN-OHL-S-2.0 OR LicenseRef-GSys-Commercial", exactly like the rest of the
# LibreCore delta. Withholding it as tier P case 2 was drafted and then NOT
# adopted -- see architecture/ai-matrix/README.md s7.
#
# The terms are therefore left to the reader in the LICENSE files rather than
# pre-resolved here: an integrator takes CERN-OHL-S-2.0, and an operator who
# wants closed modifications, marking relief, indemnity or support reads
# LICENSE.GSys-Commercial (s3.7 addresses AI and datacentre in-house
# production directly). Election is the licensee's, and nothing here blocks
# creating, committing or publishing these files.
R   core/cvxif_g6lc_ai/**
R   core/g6lc_ai_*.sv
R   core/include/g6lc_ai_*.sv
R   corev_apu/ai_descriptor/**
R   corev_apu/src/g6lc_ai_*.sv
